 "text": "Lancelot was an Arthurian hero. He was the bravest and most handsome knight of the Round Table. He became the lover of King Arthur's queen Guinevere. Their love formed a fatal triangle. That triangle was the central conflict of the Arthurian cycle. In The Knight of the Cart, Lancelot crossed a bridge made of a sword blade to reach the captive queen and wounded himself. He freed the knights trapped in the Perilous Valley. His love for the queen helped bring about the fall of Camelot.",
 "okr": {
  "objective": "Present Lancelot as the Round Table's greatest knight and the queen's lover.",
